{
  "_readme": [
    "Sports room layout. Edit this file, then in Unity: Sports Robot > Scene Builder > Build scene.",
    "Coordinates are metres on the floor as [x, z]: x grows to the east, z grows to the north.",
    "rooms: rect = [x, z, width, depth]. Walls are built around every room; shared walls are merged.",
    "  'floor': wood | tile | rubber gives the floor a texture (tinted with floor_color). 'wall_accent' (top level) colours the band on the walls.",
    "zones: painted floor areas. 'style': basketball draws half-court lines ('hoop': the side the hoop is on); gym gives a rubber floor.",
    "  'sign_at': [x, z] + 'sign_faces' hangs the zone's name on a wall. The robot reports which zone it and each object is in.",
    "  'ceiling': true roofs a room (with a light), so the overhead camera can't see inside and the robot must go and look.",
    "doors: 'at' must sit on a room edge. A closed door blocks walking until the robot opens it.",
    "faces: north | east | south | west = the direction the object's front points (the robot stands on that side).",
    "furniture kinds: rack, cabinet, locker, bench, table, mat, hoop, goal, ball_cart, treadmill, exercise_bike, rowing_machine, bench_press, squat_rack, hurdle, box",
    "  rack / cabinet: 'levels' 1-4 creates shelf targets <id>_bottom, <id>_middle, <id>_top. A cabinet has a glass door.",
    "    'label' puts a name plate on top of a rack or cabinet.",
    "  locker: 'locked': true plus 'key': '<item id>' means the robot must bring that key. 'label' is the number on the door.",
    "  'size': [width, height, depth] overrides the default size.",
    "item kinds: ball, dumbbell, bottle, racket, bat, cone, trophy, medal, key",
    "  place an item with 'on': '<furniture or shelf id>' (shelves, lockers, carts, benches...) or 'at': [x, z] on the floor.",
    "  balls: 'size': [diameter] or [x, y, z]; 'style': basketball | soccer | tennis | panels (volleyball/handball) | rugby. 'color2' = seams / patches.",
    "  others: 'scale' resizes. rackets 'style': tennis | badminton. bats 'style': cricket | baseball. 'color2' = grip / ribbon / key tag colour.",
    "  'model': 'Assets/.../SomeModel.prefab' swaps in a downloaded 3D model; it is auto-scaled to real-life size.",
    "ids are the names the robot's brain uses, so keep them descriptive and unique."
  ],

  "name": "Sports Complex",
  "wall_height": 3.5,
  "wall_color": "#E9E4DA",

